@crew sato
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Ah. You. Cadet. Survey's on Deck 2. Don't touch the labels. Tea?
- Hello. You're new. Good. New people ask the best questions.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Tea? No? Nobody ever does. More for me.   #funny
- No, the other comet. Sorry. {me}. Hello. I was in the middle of something.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Oh, good, it's you. You're one of the few who argue with me. Keep it up.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- A good day. The array caught something odd. Odd is my favourite word.
? mood:low
- Long day. I relabelled half the specimen store. In my own hand. It helped.
== near
? habit:tea-break
- Tea break. Smoked leaf, dried kelp, a pinch of pepper. It's an acquired taste.   #funny
? habit:quiet-corner
- Shh. Thinking. It's like listening, but louder.
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I named three comets. The third one doesn't count. Don't ask why. I'll tell you anyway.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- I turned down a university post to stay out here. Best no I ever said.
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- My tea. Let me explain it. Sit down. This takes a while.   #funny

// ---- Writer 2, batch 3: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, bye, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue, hint, about, life)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning. Is it? Yes. I've been up since the array pinged. Tea?   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- {me}. Where have you... never mind. You're here. I had a question. I've lost it.   #funny

== bye
- Go on. I'm thinking. No, stay. No, go. Sorry. Bye.   #funny

== near
? habit:gardener
- I help in the garden now. Cruz says I water the labels. I don't. Often.   #funny
? place:chartroom
- Look at this. No, this. The pattern. Mori sees it too. Mori sees everything.

== invite
- Observatory night? Bring questions. Good ones. Bad ones are also fine.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Tasting night. I'm bringing my tea. Somebody has to be brave. Come and be brave.   #funny

== accept
- Yes. Good. Remind me. I'll forget. I won't. I might.   #funny
- Yes. I'll bring the tea. Don't make that face.   #funny

== decline
- No. That's a full sentence, but I'm sorry anyway. The array needs me.
? weekday:sat|sun
- My rest day. I'm resting. In the lab. It's restful there. Monday?   #funny

== missed
- You weren't there. Or I wasn't. Mori would know. Next time.   #funny

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. I've brewed you a tea. A special one. You needn't drink it.   #funny
? birthday:me
- My birthday. Mori remembered for me. Mori remembers everything for me.   #warm

== cue
? cue:tradition.observatory
- Did you see it last night? The faint one, low down? No? Nobody did. I'll show you.

== hint
- {me}. A minute, later? I've something to say. Not about tea. Well. Not mostly.

== about
? aff:mori:friend
- Mori runs the labs. I run everyone. Mori runs me too. Don't tell her I know.   #funny

== life
? tier>=friend
- People think I'm brilliant. I'm stubborn. Out here, the two look almost the same.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 6: bubbles (smalltalk, rumour), at most one in five about work. 60 characters.
== smalltalk
- Tea? No? More for me.   #funny
- Odd is my favourite word.
- Shh. Thinking. It's loud.   #funny
- The third comet doesn't count.   #funny
- Where's my mug? Mori?   #funny

== rumour
- Ah. Middle of the story. Here.
- Interesting. Very odd. Listen.

// Writer 4, batch 12: goodbyes (leaving:you), packing (leaving:soon) and letters after they've moved on.
== feel
? leaving:soon
- Packing. The samples are labelled. The tea is not negotiable.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- Ah. You. I'm leaving. A post at a survey station. No. Don't make the tea.
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- You drank my tea once. Voluntarily. Nobody else has. I won't forget it.   #warm

== letter
- The station has a lab and a window. The tea here is weak. I've brought my own. Obviously.
? tier>=friend
- Found a good rock today. Labelled it in my own hand. Thought of the Wren's specimen store.

// ---- Pillar 5 Step 4 (head writer W2): star logging (24t, E3). Every third log; and Day 19 (the sensor array),
// your logging paid off. Kind 'cue', flags stars.talk / stars.paid.
== cue
? flag:stars.talk
- You've been logging! Three new points. Do you know what that's worth?
- Your logs are good. Neat. Better than mine, frankly.   #funny
? flag:stars.paid
- Your star logs helped calibrate the array. Your name's on the report.   #warm

// W3, Wren talks (RA's talk panel): when they give a talk
== talk.open
- Right. You all saw it. Tonight: {title}. Don't pretend you were eating.
== talk.answer
- Good question. Write it down. Then write the answer down. That's Survey.
== talk.listen
- No questions? Then tea. Survey's tea. Nobody else will drink it.

// ---- SW2, patch 0.92.3 item 15: her own Talk a while card frames (FX13: main characters skip the shared ones)
== talk.start
- Yes. Good. Talk. I was halfway through a thought. It'll keep.
- Oh, good. Someone to explain things to. Sit. This might take a while.   #funny
- Fine. Ten minutes. The array can wait. The array always waits.
? tier>=friend
- Ah. You. Good. I've been saving a question for you. I've lost it. Sit anyway.   #warm
- Oh, good, it's you. You ask the right wrong questions. Go on.   #warm
?

== talk.sit
- Sit. Move the notebooks. Gently. They're in an order. Mine.
- There's a chair under those samples. Probably. Yes. Sit.   #funny
- Sit down. Tea? No? Nobody ever does. Sit anyway.   #funny

== talk.filler
- Mm. Sorry. I was thinking about dust. Carry on. I'm listening. Mostly.   #funny
- The sky's doing nothing at all tonight. Lovely. Honest work.
- Where was I? No. Where were you? You were saying something. Good.   #funny
- Interesting. No, not you. That label. Never mind. You too, though.   #funny
- I like this. Thinking out loud with someone. It's faster.
- Mm. Mori would say I've stopped listening. I haven't. Not quite.   #funny

== talk.end
- Good. That was useful. I'll think about it at three in the morning.   #funny
- Right. Back to it. Thank you. That helped. I'm not sure how. Yet.
- Good talk. I've forgotten half of it already. The good half stays.   #funny
- That was nice. Don't tell Mori I said nice. She'll write it down.   #funny
- Off you go. Come and argue with me again soon. You're good at it.   #warm

== talk.stop
- Fine. Go. I'll finish the thought on my own. Badly.   #funny
- Yes, yes. Later. I'll remember. I won't. Remind me.   #funny
- Off you go. Mind the labels on your way out.

== talk.go.shift
- The array. Sorry. It's pinging. It's always pinging when I'm talking.
- Back to the lab. Mori's giving me the look. You can't see it. I can.   #funny

== talk.go.bed
- Bed. Mori's orders. I'm obeying. Tonight. Don't spread it about.   #funny
- I'm tired. I'm smiling at things. That's my sign. Goodnight.

== talk.go.trad
- {trad}'s starting. Come up. Bring questions. Good ones. Bad ones too.
- Sorry. {trad}. I said I'd be there. I'm only a little late. Yet.   #funny

// ---- ZW1 (writer), patch 0.92.5 item 5: more chat-card openers, so a tap doesn't repeat (FX13's no-repeat).
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance
- Oh, good. {me}. Tea? Fine. Just checking. I'll ask again.   #funny
- {me}. I had a thought about the third comet. It still doesn't count.   #funny
- Ah. You. Don't touch the labels. I know you wouldn't. Hello.   #funny
- {hi}. Survey's found something. Possibly. Probably nothing. Exciting.
- {me}! Good. I needed someone to say "really?" at the right moment.   #funny
- Hello. Mid-thought. Hold on. Gone. Hello, {me}.   #funny
